# Step 13: Can you use Starlette directly?

Yes.

Example:

```python
from starlette.applications import Starlette
from starlette.responses import JSONResponse
from starlette.routing import Route

async def homepage(request):
    return JSONResponse({"hello": "world"})

app = Starlette(routes=[
    Route("/", homepage)
])
```

This works, but you don't get:

* Automatic validation
* Swagger UI
* OpenAPI docs
* Dependency injection
* Pydantic integration

You have to build those features yourself.

---

# Step 14: FastAPI vs Starlette

| Feature                 | Starlette | FastAPI        |
| ----------------------- | --------- | -------------- |
| ASGI framework          | ✅         | Uses Starlette |
| Routing                 | ✅         | Uses Starlette |
| Requests                | ✅         | Re-exports     |
| Responses               | ✅         | Re-exports     |
| Middleware              | ✅         | Uses Starlette |
| WebSockets              | ✅         | Uses Starlette |
| Background Tasks        | ✅         | Uses Starlette |
| Static Files            | ✅         | Uses Starlette |
| Pydantic Validation     | ❌         | ✅              |
| Dependency Injection    | ❌         | ✅              |
| OpenAPI                 | ❌         | ✅              |
| Swagger UI              | ❌         | ✅              |
| Automatic Serialization | ❌         | ✅              |

